{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1375832-christmas-themed-courts","id":1375832,"title":"Christmas-themed Courts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-20T10:37:37-07:00","id":1375832,"title":"Christmas-themed Courts","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I know that this question is very out of left field, but here it goes. <br /> <br /> Suppose you had a freehold based somewhere in the far north. And let\u2019s say this freehold has a Christmas theme and is populated by changelings approximating the figures of Christmas/Yule lore (i.e., Santa, Mrs. Claus, Rudolph, etc.). What does you think the different courts should be?<br /> <br /> Should they reflect variations of the winter season? Should they revolve around different Christmas customs? Maybe different types of Christmas gift bringers?<br /> <br /> Any ideas would be appreciated, no matter how silly or absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25750-holy-hell-thats-hot","name":"Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T13:02:18-07:00","id":1375847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy-Hell-Thats-Hot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1375832-christmas-themed-courts#post1375832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I know that this question is very out of left field, but here it goes.<br /> <br /> Suppose you had a freehold based somewhere in the far north. And let\u2019s say this freehold has a Christmas theme and is populated by changelings approximating the figures of Christmas/Yule lore (i.e., Santa, Mrs. Claus, Rudolph, etc.). What does you think the different courts should be?<br /> <br /> Should they reflect variations of the winter season? Should they revolve around different Christmas customs? Maybe different types of Christmas gift bringers?<br /> <br /> Any ideas would be appreciated, no matter how silly or absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If it is really far in the north, I would make a combination of existing courts: Winter Court and Winter Lag, both have different views on winter.<br /> <br /> Thematically it would be better served by two first edition courts: Dawn and Dusk and some Common/Royal Winter contracts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-20-2020, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T18:29:43-07:00","id":1397416,"title":"","content":"In &quot;Christianity the Origin of a Pagan Religion&quot; by Philippe Walter I read that Father Christmas has an opposite number known as Hellequin, an emaciated figure that drives a cart pulled by skeleton horses. Father Christmas heads the Court of Plenty, while Hellequin leads the Court of Famine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T19:07:07-07:00","id":1397420,"title":"","content":"@Holy-Hell-That\u2019s-Hot would you like an answer based on what I know of Changeling: the Dreaming or would that be useless to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T19:33:54-07:00","id":1398103,"title":"","content":"A Motley of Christmas-themed Changelings with a Keeper that was basically Santa could be a really neat concept. A Reindeer Beast, some Wizened Elves, maybe a Wintry Elemental, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25438-justasplanned","name":"JustAsPlanned","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}